# UX context

Written for the AI to read **before** generating anything and to be checked **against** afterwards. Stakeholders read the synthesis and the decks; this file is the same knowledge turned into constraints. Every line cites its source.

## Constraints from research

One line each, as a rule a generator can obey: "Users abandon setup when asked for details they don't have to hand (I-3)". Not "users found setup challenging".

## Mental model and intent paths

How users think about this domain, what they come to do, and the order they expect to do it in. This drives the IA, which drives the flows, which drive the screens.

## Interaction standards

Confirm or undo? Dense or sparse? Expert or first-time optimised? Each with its reason.

## Words users use

| Users say | Not | Notes |
|---|---|---|

## Conditions of use

Interrupted, on a phone in transit, under audit, sharing a screen with a customer: how the design accounts for each.

## Change log

Dated, one line per change, with what prompted it.
